 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to wrongful towing",
    "basePrintNo": "S4522",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4522-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §241-a, add §241-c, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4522\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to wrongful towing\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide an administrative remedy for persons whose vehicle is wrong-\nfully towed.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nUnder this bill, a person whose vehicle was wrongfully towed in New York\nCity will have recourse against the Parking Violations Bureau or the\nresponsible agent by having the right to appear before a panel of admin-\nistrative law judges, established under the 1987 Improper Dunning Stat-\nute, which shall be empowered to order the correction of records, the\nrefund of any fee paid to release the wrongfully towed vehicle and\nreimbursement for out-of-pocket expenses the motorist incurred in fight-\ning the wrongful tow.\n\nA wrongful tow is defined to include the towing of a person's vehicle:\nfor a fine or penalty for a parking violation previously satisfied or\nwrongfully imposed; for a parking violation which the person is in the\nprocess of contesting with the bureau; for inaccurately being deemed a\nscofflaw; for illegal parking, which was properly licensed, insured or\nregistered at the time of the tow.\n\nAppearing before the panel, the motorist shall be required to submit\nproof which may include a copy of a receipt, money order or check, a\ncopy of a decision by an administrative law judge, a police report or a\ncopy of a current registration, license or insurance.\n\nTo ensure that records are corrected and maintained, if the person's\nvehicle happens to be towed a second or subsequent time for the same\nreason as the first wrongful tow, then the motorist would be entitled to\ndouble the amount of his out-of-pocket expenses.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapters 338 and 339 of the laws of 1987 (improper dunning statute)\nestablished a mechanism whereby motorist could challenge notices from\nthe NYC PVB demanding payment for previously satisfied or wrongfully\nimposed tickets and to seek compensation for expenses incurred while\ntrying to prove his/her innocence. This law was enacted because the PBVB\nwas dunning motorists for tickets that were dismissed as well as for\nsummonses that had already been paid but not recorded.  It has come to\nthe attention of the sponsor, that wrongful towing has become a wide\nscale problem. The vehicles of motorists are being towed after they have\npaid their fines and penalties in question or while they are contesting\nthe subject summons. Additionally, other motorists are victims because\nthey were incorrectly deemed a scofflaw. This occurs all too frequently\neither because of improper data entry or record keeping by the PVB.\nWhile their vehicles are being wrongfully towed, the frustrated motorist\ndoes not have adequate recourse to address this wrong. Hence, this bill\nextends the mechanism provided in the Improper Dunning Compensation Law\naffording the motorist the right to address this wrong.\n\nThe enactment of this measure will strengthen existing remedies and\nallow for motorists to obtain the timely relief the Legislature intended\nwith the enactment of the earlier reform legislation. Additionally, It\nwill provide an incentive to the appropriate agencies or officials to\nmaintain and administer accurate records.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2003-2004: S4121 - 3rd Reading Calendar\n2002: S6860 - Referred to Transportation  \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  To be\ndetermined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of November next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
